          "justification": "Contains React or browser DOM adaptation behind Writer command and model boundaries; no native LibreOffice source file is claimed as its owner. Viewport-bounded owned popup placement and scrolling are covered by geometry and responsive command reachability checks; complete native behavior remains unverified. Existing nested popup consumes keyboard input only in the nearest owning popup: one Enter/Space dispatch and one prefix append per key. Owned regression and real Chromium Writer ruler toggle evidence cover this bounded adapter contract; complete native menu/mnemonic behavior remains unverified. Existing pointer submenu opening focuses its popup without item preselection; keyboard opening preselects the first item. Unselected popup boundary navigation and no-command Return dismissal are covered with owned cases and real Chromium Writer interaction. Native popup/window focus maps to DOM popup/item focus; full disabled traversal defaults, pointer timers and mnemonics remain unverified. Existing root pointer opening focuses the unselected popup; keyboard Up/Down/Return opening preselects its first eligible entry, with Space retained as the browser activation adapter. Active-popup reuse and one-shot focus requests preserve current child selection and later resource rerenders. Owned regressions and actual Chromium Status Bar toggles cover this bounded contract; saved document focus, platform disabled traversal, F10/Alt, mnemonics and native pointer timers remain unverified. Existing menus retain a connected external DOM focus owner across root/submenu changes and restore it on root cancellation or before command dispatch. Command teardown synchronously unmounts popup controls before Execute, preserving focus acquired by a new dialog. Focus transfer outside cancels without restoring over its new owner. Owned callback-time popup/focus assertions and actual Chromium Writer editor/dialog/control checks cover this bounded lifecycle; no-owner nat