          "justification": "Imports supported Writer paragraph, style, list, font, hyperlink, whitespace, alignment, and character-property elements through canonical SwDoc operations. Known unsupported content structures are rejected; unrelated style families remain explicitly ignored and unclaimed. Family-first lookup and separate paragraph/text name maps now reproduce bounded family-plus-name identity. Five context inputs and six literal real ODT cases in forward/reverse declaration order verify direct and parent resolution, same-name common/automatic families, Standard/Heading identities, paragraph geometry, effective inline properties and scope through export/reimport. The old wrong-family Heading rejection fixture now verifies no paragraph-property leak against an absent paragraph definition. Import/export suites are decomposed without changing prior assertions. Common-versus-automatic container ownership, display-name identity, duplicate selection, cycles/defaults and wider semantic contracts remain unverified; this is no whole-module promotion. XMLStylesContext retains style leaf references per container; Writer retains independent common and active automatic references and replaces the automatic context when a new container is encountered. Direct lookup checks the active automatic family/name first; automatic and common parents resolve only through common definitions. Found automatic deltas survive missing parents; missing paragraph references keep the default paragraph. Context ownership assertions and fifteen literal real ODT cases verify legal common/automatic collisions, same-name parents, independent families, named-only chains, empty/missing parents, stream replacement and common-only default publication through export/reimport. The previously source-invalid automatic-parent list export chain now puts its inherited base in common styles; exact pinned tdf114287 geometry remains unchanged across package cycles. This export bridge and broader named document-model ownership still require separate architecture audit; no whole-module parity promotion. For the existing LABEL_ALIGNMENT mode and LISTTAB/SPACE/NOTHING separators, source-owned xmlnumi parsing now retains zero defaults and MM100 fields with native Converter grammar/failure and SHRT bounds. The MM100 import port now carries both independent native geometry groups; the earlier legacy-to-alignment Twip emulation is removed. Writer numbering property conversion follows unosett.cxx signed MM100/Twip ratios; export projects native MM100 and delegates CM serialization to XML/SAX. ODF 1.3 XML emits explicit label-alignment mode and retains standard command geometry; indents are nonzero-only and tab position is exported only for LISTTAB with a positive value. Context/core assertions and eleven literal common/automatic ODT cases plus both default command marker families verify native quantization, conditional XML and manual reopen state. Full numbering/UNO, legacy position mode/property ownership, NEWLINE extensions, other XML units/versions, defaults and wider obligations remain unverified; no whole-module promotion. Declared levels retain independent native legacy and alignment geometry with zero defaults; only exact label-alignment selects modern mode. SvxNumberFormat in editeng owns positional state, signed widths and mode-dependent getters; Writer inherits and copies all fields. xmlnumi owns level/property contexts and MM100 legacy parsing/assembly. Writer conversion precedes core application, and xmlnume emits the selected group with native signs and omission predicates. Thirteen literal common/automatic ODT cases verify mode spellings/absence, child presence, independent state, signed/bounded/partial/invalid legacy fields, exact XML and reopen. Clone and browser snapshots preserve inactive fields; primitive browser geometry selects the active group. Full line layout, numbering families, extensions and wider contracts/defaults remain separately unverified. No whole-module promotion. Source-ordered XML declarations now replace complete levels on a native modern Arabic base rule; omitted and empty rules retain base defaults, duplicates apply in order, and a rejected SymbolTextDistance stops later replacements while preserving prior levels. Writer owns the copy/validate/Set boundary. A bounded extracted C++ probe compares 17 ordered cases / 170 complete level states; real common/automatic ODT tests cover empty/omitted/repeated levels, independent position modes, signed distance failure, clone and browser snapshot retention, marker projections and export/reopen. Accepted MM100 distance 32767 quantizes to 32768 on export and is rejected on reopen as in the pinned sources. Full UNO ownership, outline/legacy base factories, continuous numbering, numbering families/fonts/extensions, full formatter behavior remain separate unverified obligations; no whole-module promotion. The supported list-style and declaration contexts now belong to xmlnumi. SvxXMLListStyleContext retains source-created leaf references and reads GetLevel/GetProperties at publication; levels missing their index or outside native capacity are skipped before properties are read. Optional Arabic format defaults to 1 and absent/empty bullet chars preserve the zero marker port. Present indices follow native byte-string decimal toInt32 prefix/sign/control-whitespace and overflow-to-zero semantics; nonpositive values normalize to level zero. Unrelated list child subtrees are ignored, with an explicit ignore-context adaptation for the current strict known-token SAX dispatcher; native image numbering and unsupported numeric families remain explicit errors. Direct native-context ownership/default assertions and literal common/automatic ODT/copy/snapshot/export/reopen cases cover this bounded correction. Wider marker prefix/suffix/start/display-level/font/graphics contracts, native UNO property breadth, global null dispatch and full list/style ownership remain unverified; no whole-module promotion. Known-null child fallback now creates a concrete inert SvXMLImportContext; unknown-null fallback reuses the actual parent reference. Unknown start/end dispatch uses independent hooks, preventing premature list/style/URI publication through known end callbacks. The old list known-child ignore adapters are removed. Three compiled traces / 37 reference/event entries from unmodified pinned dispatch bodies verify nested parent reuse, inert subtrees, explicit unknown contexts and sibling continuation. Direct context and literal ODT font/property/table/style/list cases verify native unrelated-child ignoring and supported descendants inside unknown wrappers; explicit cell list/section/nested-table errors remain until those native features are implemented. Root severe-error timing, namespace rewind, token completeness, remaining ignore adapters and wider import contracts remain unverified; no whole-module promotion. ODF marker transport preserves raw affixes, native byte-int start/display normalization, ordered style/loext ListFormat aliases (including empty strings), generated available-level clamp and final UNO SetListFormat compatibility overwrite for existing Arabic/bullet levels. Standard ODF 1.3 export is owned by SvxXMLNumRuleExport and coherent per-level records, with nonempty affixes, signed StartWith narrowing and clamped display omission; raw patterns retain native standard-format approximation on reopen. Sixteen literal common/automatic cases plus signed start/zero parent projection verify state, visible labels, owned clones, Worker v16, selected XML and reopen. A bounded compiled oracle matches 144 declarations, 144 applied states and 144 export attribute sets from unmodified pinned excerpts. ASCII string shims, modern/no-build-id input, Arabic/bullet and standard ODF only; ancient OOo suffix correction depends on absent generator/build-id metadata APIs and remains unresolved. Full native build, wider numbering families/fonts/legal/out