ot trigger the no-rule/list-level export diagnostic. Literal native attribute predicates and real ODT/Worker/reopen/undo tests cover this dependency slice;full XMLStyleExport inheritance fallback,UNO style machinery,style-name encoding,outline export,automatic/direct-outline properties and native lifetime/compatibility remain separately unverified. IO settings and Worker16/ODF1.3 remain unchanged. Iteration38 restores native document reading suppression for the existing shown-list notification path. SwDoc owns mbInReading=false and native IsInReading/SetInReading accessors; SwXMLImport brackets the existing parse lifetime and clears the flag on success or failure. List/tree operations propagate the actual document context. Worker graph16 restores direct text-node items in one complete text-node-range batch before attachment, retaining counted/restart/list identity and explicit rule type. Forty unchanged added native definitions compare60 sequences/2130 states including true/false reading, raw caches and notifications; literal genuine ODT/Worker/reopen expectations remain intact. Full native destructor/temporary notification blockers/layout/UNO/history/fields/live-style/serialization lifetime remain unverified; no whole-module promotion or registered IO change. Iteration102 materializes document-owned named paragraph collections instead of flattening common styles into direct node items. Supported own paragraph/character/list fields, raw names, parent/follow links and automatic deltas survive graph16, ODT cycles and actual history. Native name lookup and bounded custom CopyTextColl preserve destination ownership and manual rule handling; the prior builtin copy adapter remains unchanged. Literal zero/per-axis list masks and the project tdf114287 fixture distinguish inherited margins from hard rule overrides. Writer export retains original named parents and emits actual direct numbering items; generic legacy export remains compatible. Default paragraph items are retain